====================================================================================================
8. Map back to BOTH printed relations (prereg §5)
====================================================================================================
  printed spin-fluid   : s^2 = 1/2 s_ik s^ik = (1/8) n^2      [entry 10 L121]
  printed Dirac        : <s^2> = (3/4) n^2                    [entry 10 L113]
  C6 above derived that these are the SAME quantity, so both are compared to the same number.

derived exchange coefficient, non-relativistic -3/8
derived exchange coefficient, ultrarelativistic -3/16

  vs printed +1/8 : neither limit reproduces it (sign differs; magnitude differs)
  vs printed +3/4 : neither limit reproduces it (sign differs; magnitude differs)
  The NR magnitude 3/8 is exactly half of the printed 3/4, with the opposite sign;
  the UR magnitude 3/16 is 1.5x the printed 1/8, with the opposite sign.

